[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds every report about a wrong date and calls them one issue with
one fix queued. The reports describe three problems, and one fix covers only the first. Each
problem now has its own ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

## parser

The shared parser reads every date month first. All our tenants write the day first, so a
booking for 2 March comes out as 3 February. This covers app and email reports from every
tenant, and form reports from tenants on booking-v2.

## hint

The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type the month first, as
the hint tells them, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. A parser fix
leaves these broken. The hint has to change. Only tenants on booking-v3 who book through the
form hit it.

## oneDayMove

None of these reports has a day and month swapped. The booking lands one day early, or on a
different day depending on where the reader is: "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
Toronto got Monday." That points at time zones, not at the parser. The desk listed them in
`desk-notes.json` as a one-day move. The desk counts a report where it is filed and footnotes
what it was read as (`readAs` in `causes.ts`), so these stay in the `parser` row as well as
having a row and a ticket of their own.

The tenant and the channel decide a report's cause (`causes.ts`). Intake's tag guesses from the
reporter's browser and disagrees with the cause often, so this page does not use it.

